  "editorial": "A nested scan is quadratic. A set of the allowed values makes each membership expected constant time, and walking left preserves the order the caller already had. Building the set inside the loop would throw the gain away.",
  "reference_solution": "def solve(left, right):\n    allowed = set(right)\n    return [item for item in left if item in allowed]\n"
